    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d474">

                <pb facs="0706" n="624" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg624"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.1051/50</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Ramer</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-02-17"><hi rendition="#italic">February 17,
                        1925</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 204</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Department’s telegram
                    No. 26, February 10, 3 p.m., regarding the plan for the establishment of a
                    Constabulary in Nicaragua, there is transmitted herewith a copy of the plan as
                    outlined in the telegram.<anchor n="7" xml:id="d474-f1"/></p>
                <p>It is assumed that you will transmit to the Department a copy of the plan as
                    presented to the Nicaraguan Government, together with your note presenting the
                    plan and any other correspondence regarding it.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph
                            C. Grew</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d474-a1.xml" xpointer="d474-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d474-f1" n="7" xml:id="d474-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram not printed. This copy of the plan incorporates the Department’s
                    amendments to an earlier draft transmitted by the Legation.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
